# Our own English translation of Dala'il al-Khayrat, made from the Arabic. One line per Arabic paragraph.
# "Muhammad" is rendered "our master Muhammad" where the Arabic has sayyidina.
B = "O Allah, send blessings upon our master Muhammad"
EN = {}

EN[1] = [
 "Section on how to send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ",
 "In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate.",
 "May Allah send blessings upon our master and patron Muhammad, upon his family and companions, and grant them peace.",
 f"{B}, his wives and his descendants, as You sent blessings upon our master Ibrahim; and bless our master Muhammad, his wives and his descendants, as You blessed the family of our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 f"{B} and his family, as You sent blessings upon our master Ibrahim; and bless our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You blessed the family of our master Ibrahim among all the worlds. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon our master Ibrahim; and bless our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You blessed our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 f"{B}, the unlettered Prophet, and upon the family of our master Muhammad.",
 f"{B}, Your servant and Your Messenger.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, bless our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You blessed our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, have mercy upon our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You had mercy upon our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, show tenderness to our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You showed tenderness to our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, grant peace to our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You granted peace to our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad; have mercy upon our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad; and bless our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You sent blessings, mercy and blessing upon our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim among all the worlds. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 f"{B}, the Prophet, and upon his wives, the Mothers of the Believers, his descendants and the people of his house, as You sent blessings upon our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, bless our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You blessed our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, Spreader of the spread-out earths, Maker of the raised heavens, Who shapes hearts upon their natures, the wretched and the blessed alike: place Your noblest blessings, Your growing favours and the gentleness of Your tenderness upon our master Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger; the opener of what was closed and the seal of what went before; who proclaims the truth by the truth and crushes the armies of falsehood; who, as he was charged, carried Your command in obedience to You, eager for Your pleasure, mindful of Your revelation, keeping Your covenant, pressing on to carry out Your command, until he lit a flame for every seeker. Through him Allah's favours reach those worthy of them. By him hearts were guided after plunging into trials and sin, and he made bright the clear signposts, the shining rulings and the lights of Islam. He is Your trusted one, the faithful; the keeper of Your treasured knowledge; Your witness on the Day of Judgement; the one You sent as a favour, and Your Messenger with the truth as a mercy.",
 "O Allah, make room for him in Your Garden of Eden, and reward him from Your bounty with goodness multiplied, pure and unclouded, from the triumph of Your ready reward and the abundance of Your continuous giving.",
 "O Allah, raise his building above the buildings of all people, honour his abode and his welcome with You, perfect his light for him, and reward him for Your sending him with testimony that is accepted and speech that is pleasing, a man of just word, decisive judgement and mighty proof.",
 "Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet. O you who believe, send blessings upon him and greet him with abundant peace.",
 "Here I am, O Allah my Lord, at Your service. The blessings of Allah, the Kind, the Merciful, and of the angels brought near, the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs and the righteous, and of everything that glorifies You, O Lord of the worlds, be upon our master Muhammad son of ʿAbdullah, the Seal of the Prophets, master of the Messengers, leader of the God-fearing and Messenger of the Lord of the worlds; the witness, the bearer of good news, the caller to You by Your leave, the light-giving lamp, upon him be peace.",
 "O Allah, place Your blessings, Your grace and Your mercy upon the master of the Messengers, the leader of the God-fearing and the Seal of the Prophets, our master Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, the leader in goodness, the guide to goodness and the Messenger of mercy.",
 "O Allah, raise him to a praised station, for which the first and the last will long to share his place.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, bless our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You blessed our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 f"{B}, upon his family, his companions, his children, his wives, his descendants, the people of his house, his relatives by marriage, his helpers, his followers, those who love him and his whole community, and upon us together with them all, O Most Merciful of the merciful.",
 f"{B} as many times as those who have blessed him; send blessings upon our master Muhammad as many times as those who have not; send blessings upon our master Muhammad as You commanded us to; and send blessings upon him as You love him to be blessed.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad, as You commanded us to send blessings upon him.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad, as he deserves.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad, as You love and are pleased with for him.",
 "O Allah, Lord of our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, send blessings upon our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, and give our master Muhammad the high rank and the Wasilah in Paradise.",
 "O Allah, Lord of our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, reward our master Muhammad ﷺ as he deserves.",
 f"{B}, the family of our master Muhammad and the people of his house.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad until nothing of blessing remains,",
 "and have mercy upon our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad until nothing of mercy remains,",
 "and bless our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad until nothing of blessing remains,",
 "and grant peace to our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad until nothing of peace remains.",
 f"{B} among the first,",
 "and send blessings upon our master Muhammad among the last,",
 "and send blessings upon our master Muhammad among the prophets,",
 "and send blessings upon our master Muhammad among the Messengers,",
 "and send blessings upon our master Muhammad in the highest assembly until the Day of Judgement.",
 "O Allah, give our master Muhammad the Wasilah, the excellence, the honour and the lofty rank.",
 "O Allah, I have believed in our master Muhammad without seeing him, so do not deny me the sight of him in the Gardens. Grant me his companionship, take my soul upon his religion, and give me to drink from his Pool a full, smooth and pleasant drink, after which we will never thirst again. You have power over all things.",
 "O Allah, convey to the soul of our master Muhammad greetings and peace from me.",
 "O Allah, just as I have believed in our master Muhammad without seeing him, do not deny me the sight of him in the Gardens.",
 "O Allah, accept the great intercession of our master Muhammad, raise his lofty rank, and give him what he asks in the next life and in this, as You gave our master Ibrahim and our master Musa.",
 f"{B} and the family of our master Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim; and bless our master Muhammad and the family of our master Muhammad, as You blessed our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, send blessings, peace and grace upon our master Muhammad, Your Prophet and Messenger,",
 "and upon our master Ibrahim, Your intimate friend and chosen one, and our master Musa, to whom You spoke and with whom You conversed,",
 "and our master ʿIsa, Your spirit and Your word; and upon all Your angels, Messengers and prophets, the best of Your creation, Your chosen ones, Your elect and Your friends among the people of Your earth and Your heaven.",
 "May Allah send blessings upon our master Muhammad as many as His creation, as much as pleases Him, as heavy as His Throne and as vast as the ink of His words, as he deserves, whenever those who remember mention him and whenever the heedless forget to; and upon the people of his house and his pure kin, and grant them abundant peace.",
 f"{B}, his wives and descendants, all the prophets and Messengers, the angels and those brought near, and all the righteous servants of Allah, as many as the drops the sky has rained since You built it; and send blessings upon our master Muhammad as many as the plants the earth has grown since You spread it out,",
 "and send blessings upon our master Muhammad as many as the stars in the sky, for You have counted them,",
 "and send blessings upon our master Muhammad as many as the breaths souls have taken since You created them,",
 "and send blessings upon our master Muhammad as many as all You have created and will create and all that Your knowledge encompasses, and many times more.",
 "O Allah, send blessings upon them as many as Your creation, as much as pleases You, as heavy as Your Throne, as vast as the ink of Your words, and as far as Your knowledge and Your signs reach.",
 "O Allah, send blessings upon them that surpass and exceed the blessings of all creation upon them, as Your excellence surpasses all Your creation.",
 "O Allah, send blessings upon them that last forever, continuing through the passing of nights and days, unbroken, never ending or ceasing through the passing of nights and days, as many as every downpour and drizzle.",
 "O Allah, send blessings upon our master Muhammad, Your Prophet, our master Ibrahim, Your intimate friend, and all Your prophets and chosen ones among the people of Your earth and Your heaven, as many as Your creation, as much as pleases You, as heavy as Your Throne, as vast as the ink of Your words, as far as Your knowledge reaches and as heavy as all Your creatures: blessings repeated forever, as many as Your knowledge has counted, filling all that Your knowledge has counted and many times more, blessings that grow beyond and exceed the blessings of all creation upon them, as Your excellence surpasses all Your creation.",
 "Then make this du'a, for it is hoped to be answered, if Allah wills, after sending blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ:",
 "O Allah, make me one of those who hold fast to the religion of Your Prophet, our master Muhammad ﷺ, who honour what he made sacred, raise high his word, keep his covenant and his trust, support his party and his call, add to his followers and his community, arrive among his company, and never depart from his way and his Sunnah.",
 "O Allah, I ask You to hold fast to his Sunnah, and I seek refuge in You from turning away from what he brought.",
 "O Allah, I ask You for the best of what our master Muhammad, Your Prophet and Messenger ﷺ, asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the worst of what our master Muhammad, Your Prophet and Messenger ﷺ, sought refuge in You from.",
 "O Allah, protect me from the evil of trials, keep me safe from every affliction, set right what is outward and inward in me, cleanse my heart of rancour and envy, and leave me owing no one.",
 "O Allah, I ask You to take up the best of what You know and leave the worst of what You know. I ask You to provide for me, to be content with enough, to find clarity out of every doubt, to be right in every argument, to be just in anger and in contentment, to accept what destiny brings, to be moderate in poverty and in wealth, to be humble in word and deed, and to be truthful in earnest and in jest.",
 "O Allah, I have sins between me and You, and sins between me and Your creation.",
 "O Allah, forgive those that are against You, take upon Yourself on my behalf those that are against Your creation, and make me free of need through Your bounty. You are vast in forgiveness.",
 "O Allah, light my heart with knowledge, use my body in Your obedience, free my innermost from trials,",
 "occupy my thoughts with reflection,",
 "protect me from the evil whisperings of Shaytan,",
 "and keep me safe from him, O Most Merciful, so that he has no power over me.",
]
